  "acrm---key-feature-1-content": "<h3>Starts on the store event you pick</h3><p>Connects to Shopify, WooCommerce or BigCommerce through their APIs. A paid order or a new customer signup starts each run, and every run is saved as a row you can search.</p>",
  "awb---how-to-step-3-des": "Put every SKU in one sheet with its supplier, the supplier's order inbox and the unit cost. Workflows that route orders or report margin read from this table, and any SKU missing a supplier is flagged for you instead of guessed.",
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Store Automation Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is ecommerce automation?\", \"a\": \"Ecommerce automation is software that runs the repeat steps of an online store without someone clicking through them. A store event, such as a paid order or a customer going quiet, triggers a rule. The app then sends the message or holds the order for a person.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you build ecommerce automation software?\", \"a\": \"Describe one repeat job in Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder'>AI automation builder</a>, with the store event that starts it and the person who signs off. A request to split each Shopify order by supplier and email every supplier its own lines becomes working ecommerce automation software. It comes with a supplier table you can edit and a log of every run.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the best ecommerce automation tools?\", \"a\": \"Pick by how much of the logic is yours. Zapier, Make, and n8n link a store to other apps with prebuilt steps. Rules that read your own supplier table or margin numbers fit better in an app of their own, built with Emergent from a description and run with no task cap.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does automated dropshipping work?\", \"a\": \"The store takes the order and the payment but holds no stock. Each line goes to the supplier that carries it, and the supplier ships straight to the customer. Automated dropshipping does that forwarding and copies the supplier's tracking number back to the order.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a dropshipping automation platform handle?\", \"a\": \"It should split a cart that holds products from two suppliers into separate purchase orders. A good dropshipping automation platform also keeps each supplier's order inbox on file and alerts you when a supplier has not shipped within the window you agreed on.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is ecommerce marketing automation?\", \"a\": \"Ecommerce marketing automation sends messages because of what a customer did, not on a date someone picked. A first purchase, an abandoned cart or a birthday month each starts its own sequence. Good marketing automation for ecommerce also stops a sequence the moment the customer buys.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you set up ecommerce email automation?\", \"a\": \"Start with one trigger and one email, such as a thank-you after a second order. In ecommerce email marketing automation, every promotional send needs a working way to opt out under CAN-SPAM. Opt-outs have to be honored within 10 business days. Have the app check the subscription field before each send.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is ecommerce fulfillment automation?\", \"a\": \"Ecommerce fulfillment automation covers the steps between a paid order and a package at the door. It picks the warehouse or supplier and sends the customer a tracking link. Label buying and carrier choice are their own build, covered under shipping automation.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some ecommerce automation examples?\", \"a\": \"Stores automate low-stock alerts to the buyer and review requests a week after delivery. Tagging wholesale customers by order size is another. Restock purchases above a set amount can wait for an owner's sign-off through an approval workflow.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is ecommerce process automation?\", \"a\": \"Ecommerce process automation looks at a whole back-office process, not one message. Month-end reconciliation of payouts against orders is a good example, since it touches several systems and needs a record of who checked what. Map the process on paper before you automate any part of it.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
